From 9c150e234d0c68ef9e9944ffc52f206e368d5131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:39:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: don't drain an uninitialized bus_reset work

brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work() runs on every removal, but drvr->bus_reset
is only initialized in brcmf_bus_started(), after the firmware is up.
When firmware loading fails (e.g. no firmware installed), PCIe removal
reaches cancel_work_sync() on a zeroed work_struct and __flush_work()
warns:

  WARNING: kernel/workqueue.c: __flush_work+... (WARN_ON(!work->func))
  brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work+0x40/0x60
  brcmf_pcie_remove+0x6c/0x140
  brcmf_pcie_setup+0x50/0x4c8

Skip the drain when the work was never initialized, as
brcmf_bus_schedule_reset() already does before arming it.

Fixes: 177a25be1195 ("wifi: brcmfmac: drain bus_reset work on device removal")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7f1e74a253b82405aecefd94c4b6a14a11d6e810)

Original-Commit: 233b8332d59940785f44154fa1b2a4b40431812d
Signed-off-by: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Assisted-By: LLM
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index 13cb6cb9655a..f1d224765c69 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -1186,7 +1186,8 @@ void brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work(struct brcmf_bus *bus_if)
 {
 	mutex_lock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 	bus_if->removing = true;
-	if (bus_if->drvr)
+	/* bus_reset is only initialized once the firmware is up. */
+	if (bus_if->drvr && bus_if->drvr->bus_reset.func)
 		cancel_work_sync(&bus_if->drvr->bus_reset);
 	mutex_unlock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 }
